demo> /help term.eol
NAME
  /term.eol - Show or set the line ending sent with commands (cr/lf/crlf/none).

CURRENT STATE
  cr

SYNOPSIS
  /term.eol {cr|lf|crlf|none|cycle}

DESCRIPTION
  What ends a line: the ending added to each line sent, how received
  output is split into lines, and whether line endings are shown.

  Sets the line ending appended to every command sent to the
  device.  Tokens: cr (\r), lf (\n), crlf (\r\n), none.
  Bare /term.eol reports the current ending.

  See also: /term.eol.rx (receive-side newline) and
  /term.eol.markers (show \r \n markers for debugging).

CONFIG
  eol = "\r"  set for the session; bare shows it

SUBCOMMANDS
  /term.eol.markers    Toggle dim visible \r \n markers in received output.
  /term.eol.rx         Show or set how received output is split into lines (auto/cr/lf/crlf).
