demo> /print === section: help required capabilities ===
  === section: help required capabilities ===
demo> /help profile.save
NAME
  /profile.save - Write the active profile to a file (default: <cfg_dir>/<cfg_stem>.profile.json).

SYNOPSIS
  /profile.save {path}

DESCRIPTION
  Saves the active profile dict to disk so the next connect auto-loads it via the profile_path/file-existence path.

  Default path is <cfg_dir>/<cfg_stem>.profile.json so the saved file co-locates with the cfg that drove the session and gets picked up automatically on reconnect.

  Warns if every command in the profile has enabled=false (typical for a freshly-fetched device dump before audit) -- saving is fine, just a nudge that audit is pending.

REQUIRED CAPABILITIES
  profile_loaded - a loaded device profile (missing)
