demo> /help cfg.load
NAME
  /cfg.load - Load a different config in this session (hot-swap).

SYNOPSIS
  /cfg.load <name>

DESCRIPTION
  Puts the session where a fresh start on that config would: what this session changed is gone, including settings, user variables, /env.set values, counters and the device profile.  A capture or a recording stops.  The port opens only if the config says auto_connect.  What you asked for at launch, such as --no-color or --quiet, still holds.
demo> /var.set GOLD_LOAD_VAR 1
  $(GOLD_LOAD_VAR) = 1
demo> /env.set GOLD_LOAD_ENV 1
    GOLD_LOAD_ENV=1
demo> /print {seq7+}
  1
demo> /term.output verbose
  verbose
demo> /cfg.load demo
Connected: DEMO
  Loaded config: demo
  normal
    $(GOLD_LOAD_VAR) - not defined
  Environment snapshot - empty
  1
  === section: rename and delete need a person ===
NAME
  /cap.rename - Rename a file in cap/ (extension kept; never overwrites).

SYNOPSIS
  /cap.rename <old> <new>

PARAMETERS
  <old>  current filename (extension optional) (required)
  <new>  new name (the extension is kept) (required)

AVAILABLE
  TUI: yes   CLI: yes (current)   MCP: no
  (MCP does not provide: interactive)
